  "- Task1: Ruling: resolve only HDMI timing aliases differing in polarity at CDRMUtils::GetModes, retaining the display-advertised CTA member : this lets Kodi's unchanged picker/whitelist select a valid timing without forced UHD or driver relaxation : cost if wrong: ordinary HDMI playback may select a different advertised polarity alias; all distinct timing/layout/rate choices must remain, and vanilla output is part of qualification.",
  "- Final: Ruling: supersede generic catalog canonicalization with a transaction- local advertised CTA alias, returning to the original timing on ordinary exit. Native GetModes, whitelist, selection and automatic range remain unchanged. Cost if wrong: a rejected alias transition could prevent DV activation; strict atomic test/real commit, retained mode blob and accepted receipt remain required.",
  "- Final: Ruling: unrelated historical branch changes remain outside this bounded review; preserve them rather than reopen the whole release. Cost if wrong: pre-existing unrelated defects are not newly ruled out.",
  "- Final: Ruling: executor owns complete-image and extended hardware journeys; reviewer did not contact machines. Cost if wrong: bounded observations cannot establish indefinite stability; retain windows and exact image receipts.",
  "- Final: Ruling: physical calibration/wire levels and every720p/limited-GUI/ fractional-display combination are not claimed certified. Preserve native catalog/timing for ordinary playback and run matched limited-range1080p controls. Cost if wrong: an untested display setup can retain a baseline defect.",
  "- Final: Ruling: unchanged render/model libraries plus executable exactness tests and physical HDMI windows are the fidelity gate, not external Dolby capture certification. Cost if wrong: an issue outside these witnesses can remain.",
